Package: ghreg
Title: Persistence Meta-Regression Adjusted for Correlated Sampling Error
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Joshua B.", "Gilbert", , "joshua_gilbert@gse.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits the Bayesian persistence meta-regression of Gilbert and
    Himmelsbach (2026) <doi:10.26300/87r9-qm15>, which regresses follow-up
    effect sizes on endline effect sizes while accounting for sampling error
    in both and for the correlation between the two sampling errors. Ignoring
    that correlation usually overstates how much intervention effects
    persist. Supports multiple effect-size pairs per study, study-specific
    sampling correlations, and sensitivity analysis over a range of assumed
    correlations. Models are fit in 'Stan' through 'rstan' or 'cmdstanr'.
